alana: Heads-up — I'm prepping a small refresh of the hello-mini quickstart to migrate the auth examples to the SDK v8 ephemeral API-key pattern (short-lived keys + rotation). This will touch docs/quickstart/hello-mini.md, samples/hello, snippets/auth.md, and our CI example. Any objections?

mike: no objections. solid idea. which CI example do you mean? the GH Actions one under .github/workflows/ci.yml?

alana: yes that one. the current CI snippet still shows a long-lived secret in env, we should show the ephemeral mint step plus a note about dedicated/private KMS differences.

kevin: also the TypeScript snippet in snippets/auth.md uses a setInterval that leaks if you recreate client instances. can we show a rotation helper instead?

sara: I can take the snippet rewrite. could you paste the minimal helper here so I can PR it into the sample app?

alana: sure, draft helper below — please trim if it's too heavy:
```js
// rotateShortLivedKey.js - minimal example
let currentKey = null;
async function rotateKey(fetchEphemeral) {
  currentKey = await fetchEphemeral();
  // your SDK accepts a setApiKey helper
  client.setApiKey(currentKey);
  // refresh ~55 minutes for a 1h token
  setTimeout(() => rotateKey(fetchEphemeral), 55 * 60 * 1000);
}
// usage: rotateKey(getEphemeralApiKeyFromCI);
```

kevin: nice, wrap in a cleanup so you dont leak timers if the app tears down. maybe return an object with stop() for tests.

